/// \defgroup grp_w1023b_ini_definition_parsers INI definition parsers: images, colours, roads, water, victory, Eva and draw options
/// \ingroup grp_ini
/// \brief Block and field parsers that turn INI text into mapped images,
///        multiplayer colours and settings, terrain roads, water settings,
///        skybox texture sets, victory-system data, Eva settings, emotion
///        nuggets, Create-a-Hero attribute binders, command buttons and two
///        W3D model draw options.
///
/// These are the parse functions an INI author triggers directly. Each one
/// is either a block parser, registered under a block keyword and called
/// when a line starts with it, or a field parser, called from a FieldParse
/// table when a field name is read. \ref INI explains both signatures and
/// \ref sub_ini_flow how a load drives them; this group adds what each
/// parser here does with its text, which keys it accepts and which
/// mistakes it rejects.
///
/// \par Block parsers in this group
/// The keyword is the first token of the line that opens the block, and the
/// field names are the names in the parser's FieldParse table, read from the
/// retail executable's own tables (the project's field table listing,
/// `reverse/fieldparse_tables.tsv`, is where to look for others).
/// | Block keyword | Parser | What it fills | Fields |
/// |---|---|---|---|
/// | MappedImage | INI::parseMappedImageDefinition | one Image in the mapped image collection | Texture, TextureWidth, TextureHeight, Coords, Status |
/// | MultiplayerColor | INI::parseMultiplayerColorDefinition | one colour of the multiplayer colour list | TooltipName, RGBColor, RGBNightColor, LivingWorldColor, LivingWorldBannerColor, AvailableInWotR |
/// | Road | INI::parseTerrainRoadDefinition | one road type of the terrain road collection | Texture, RoadWidth, RoadWidthInTexture |
/// | WaterSet | INI::parseWaterSettingDefinition | the water settings of one time of day | SkyTexture, WaterTexture, Vertex00Color, Vertex10Color, Vertex01Color, Vertex11Color, DiffuseColor, TransparentDiffuseColor, UScrollPerMS, VScrollPerMS, SkyTexelsPerUnit, WaterRepeatCount |
/// | SkyboxTextureSet | iniParseEnvironmentSkyboxTextureDefinition | one named set of five skybox textures | SkyboxTextureN, SkyboxTextureE, SkyboxTextureS, SkyboxTextureW, SkyboxTextureT |
/// | VictorySystemData | iniParseVictorySystemDefinition | the victory system's tuning values | CellSize, ScalePerLogicFrame, SubtractPerLogicFrame, CellBonusRadius |
/// | FactionVictoryData | iniParseFactionVictoryDefinition | the victory parameters of one faction | AllyDeathScaleFactor, EnemyKillScaleFactor, VictoryThreshold, MapToCellVictoryRatio, MajorUnitValue |
/// | MiscEvaData | INI::parseMiscEvaData | the Eva announcer's global settings | EnemySightedMaxVoicePositionScanRange, EnemyCampDestroyedDamageTimeoutMS, FriendlyCampDestroyedDamageTimeoutMS, MaxMillisecondsToKeepJumpToEvents, MaxMillisecondsBeforeResettingLastJumpTo, MinDistanceBetweenJumpToEvents |
///
/// \par Field parsers in this group
/// | Field | Where it sits | Parser |
/// |---|---|---|
/// | Coords, Status | MappedImage block | Image::parseImageCoords, Image::parseImageStatus |
/// | Command | CommandButton block | CommandButton::parseCommand |
/// | CopyFrom | EmotionNugget block | parseEmotionNuggetCopyFrom |
/// | Attribute | a sub-class of a CreateAHeroClass block | parseCreateAHeroBlingBinder |
/// | LodOptions | W3DHordeModelDraw module block | W3DModelDrawModuleData::parseLodOptions |
/// | AttachModel | model draw module blocks | W3DScriptedModelDrawModuleData::parseAttachModel |
///
/// \par Order matters inside a block
/// A block's fields run in the order they are written, each one reading
/// whatever the object holds at that moment. Three parsers here depend on
/// it: a mapped image's Coords line needs TextureWidth and TextureHeight
/// above it and its Status line must come after Coords; an EmotionNugget's
/// CopyFrom overwrites what the lines above it set. Their pages give the
/// details.
///
/// \par Blocks that return without reading their fields
/// Four of these block parsers have a path that returns without calling
/// INI::initFromINI and without any error: INI::parseMappedImageDefinition
/// when the mapped image collection does not exist,
/// iniParseVictorySystemDefinition and iniParseFactionVictoryDefinition when
/// the victory system does not exist (the second also when it cannot find or
/// create the faction's record; both write a debug report instead), and
/// iniParseEnvironmentSkyboxTextureDefinition when a set of that name is
/// already registered. The block's field lines are then left to the loader.
/// INI::parseLine reads the next line as a new top-level line and throws
/// "Unknown block" for a first token that is not a registered keyword, so,
/// as far as the two bodies show, a skipped block normally ends the load
/// with an error. In normal startup the engine creates the collection and
/// registers the victory system before it loads their data, so the
/// duplicate skybox name is the path an INI author can reach.
///
/// \par Modding
/// - Data-driven: every field in the table above, in INI text. Block names
///   are chosen by the data: image names, colour tooltip names, road
///   names, skybox set names and faction names.
/// - Hard-coded: the block keywords and field names (case-sensitive; a new
///   one needs code), the command-name list behind a button's Command, the
///   three level-of-detail names LOW, MEDIUM and HIGH, the six time-of-day
///   names that WaterSet accepts, the two image status names and the cap of
///   100 percent on attached-model probabilities.
/// - Where each block's file is read from depends on its owning subsystem
///   (\ref sub_ini_legend and \ref sub_ini_entry). Mapped images are the
///   exception: ImageCollection::load reads fixed directories under
///   `Data\INI\MappedImages` and passes no CRC writer. `Water.ini` and
///   `Environment.ini` are read by GameEngine::init through the CRC writer,
///   so edits to those files change the INI CRC even though water and sky
///   data only affects drawing (\ref page_modding_rules); which file holds the
///   WaterSet and SkyboxTextureSet blocks is data and is not checked here.
///   Eva's files are read by Eva's own initialisation without the writer.
/// - Logic-side data: command buttons are read by game logic as well as by
///   the UI, the victory system is a game-logic subsystem in the BFME 1
///   sources and BFME 2 saves it with the game state, and the multiplayer
///   settings include match rules such as the starting-credit presets, the
///   beacon limit and the shroud switch. Changing data like this on one
///   machine desynchronises play against unmodified clients and changes how
///   saves and replays behave (\ref page_modding_rules). This page does not
///   classify the Create-a-Hero or emotion data.
///
/// \par Remastering
/// - Colours and real numbers are parsed in the x87 single-precision mode
///   that the load entry points set, and floating-point fields are stored
///   as 32-bit values (\ref sub_ini_remaster).
/// - Image coordinates are authored in texels of a texture size that the
///   INI declares, then stored as fractions. A replacement texture with the
///   same layout therefore needs no INI change (see \ref Image).
/// - Most parsers here store numbers as written, with no conversion to the
///   logic rate. Where a value is converted (the Eva timeouts and the model
///   draw velocities and durations) the page says so.
///
/// \see INI, \ref sub_ini, \ref sub_ini_modding

/// \file CreateAHeroParseBlingBinder.cpp
/// \ingroup grp_w1023b_ini_definition_parsers
/// \brief The Create-a-Hero attribute binder field parser.
///
/// \see parseCreateAHeroBlingBinder

/// \file INIEmotionCopyFrom.cpp
/// \ingroup grp_w1023b_ini_definition_parsers
/// \brief The EmotionNugget CopyFrom field parser.
///
/// \see parseEmotionNuggetCopyFrom

/// \file INIEnvironment.cpp
/// \ingroup grp_w1023b_ini_definition_parsers
